# Lecture Notes

Four proof-focused manuscripts are maintained:

- `Lecture draft/Lecture draft.tex`: the b-calculus, Fredholm theory on
  closed manifolds and cylindrical ends, the APS spectral boundary problem,
  and K-theoretic and heat-kernel proofs of the Atiyah--Patodi--Singer theorem.
- `Lecture draft/Atiyah-Singer index theorem.tex`: elliptic operators,
  K-theoretic push-forward, heat kernels, Clifford modules, the local index
  theorem, Gauss--Bonnet, the signature theorem, almost Hermitian and almost
  Kähler geometry, the almost Dolbeault operator, and Riemann--Roch.
- `Lecture draft/Hochschild homology of b-pseudodifferential operators.tex`:
  the continuous Hochschild homology of the Laurent complete-symbol algebra
  of the b-calculus, including the filtration, Poisson differential, Laurent
  de Rham model, face decomposition, residual-operator caveat, and carefully
  scoped alternative reconstructions by Čech--de Rham descent and
  Rees--Fedosov Hochschild-chain formality.
- `Microlocal analysis/Microlocal analysis and index theory.tex` (with
  `preamble.tex`, `bibliography.tex` and `chapters/`): a single streamlined
  edition merging two sets of lecture notes by R. B. Melrose, *Introduction to
  Microlocal Analysis* (MIT, 2003) and *Lectures on Pseudodifferential
  Operators* (MIT 18.157, 2005--2006). Part I: distributions, the calculus on
  R^n, microlocalization, conormal distributions, operators on manifolds;
  Part II: isotropic and scattering calculi, traces and determinants;
  Part III: elliptic boundary problems, Hamilton--Jacobi theory, the wave
  equation and Weyl asymptotics; Part IV: index theory (homotopy invariance,
  Toeplitz operators, Bott periodicity, product-type operators, the families
  index theorem, eta forms); Part V: Hochschild homology. Notation is unified,
  draft material and empty sections of the originals are removed, and proofs
  are completed; each chapter ends with exercises and a Notes section recording
  the main corrections to the originals.

Compiled releases, with stable contents and figure lists, are available here:

- [Microlocal Analysis and Index Theory](<output/pdf/Microlocal analysis and index theory.pdf>)

- [Heat Kernels and Index Theory](<output/pdf/Atiyah-Singer index theorem.pdf>)
- [Notes on the b-Calculus and the APS Index Theorem](<output/pdf/Lecture draft.pdf>)
- [Hochschild Homology of the b-Pseudodifferential Symbol Algebra](<output/pdf/Hochschild homology of b-pseudodifferential operators.pdf>)

The July 2026 revision is a line-by-line mathematical edit of the original
lecture transcriptions. Relevant classroom discussion is retained as concise
Discussion and Question/Answer interludes; speaker attributions, unresolved
chatter, duplicated chapters, generated files, and unrelated archive material
are omitted. Definitions precede use, theorem hypotheses are explicit, and
proof gaps are filled or identified as standard input. The original diagrams
were audited against the surrounding arguments. The strongest original
blow-up, cylindrical, conormal, Mellin, parametrix, and heat-cutoff figures are
retained; new vector diagrams supplement them for symbolic, spectral, and
proof-dependency arguments where no comparable original figure existed.

## Build

From the repository root:

```sh
make
```

The build uses `latexmk` with pdfLaTeX until references, tables of contents,
and lists of figures stabilize. Intermediate files go to `tmp/pdfs/`; the
four release PDFs in `output/pdf/` are intentionally tracked.
